%H A400778 Karan Sharma, <a href="/A400778/a400778_3.png">The first 15 terms in a row, each drawn as a single-loop design, with lamps in place of dots</a>
%H A400778 Karan Sharma, <a href="/A400778/a400778.txt">Python program</a>
%F A400778 T(n,k) = T(k,n).
%F A400778 T(1,k) = 1, since any mirror in a single row of dots cuts the curve into two parts.
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(2,k) = 4^(k-1).
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(3,k) = 4^(k-1)*A001353(k).
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(4,k) = 64*T(4,k-1) - 512*T(4,k-2) for k >= 4.
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(5,k) = 256*T(5,k-1) - 11776*T(5,k-2) + 65536*T(5,k-3) - 65536*T(5,k-4) for k >= 6.
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(6,k) = 1024*T(6,k-1) - 237568*T(6,k-2) + 12582912*T(6,k-3) - 150994944*T(6,k-4) for k >= 6.
%F A400778 All five conjectures hold for k <= 22.
%F A400778 Conjecture: T(n,k) <= 4^((n-1)*(k-1)), with equality exactly when n <= 2 or k <= 2. Verified for n + k <= 17.
